    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16163" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-rŏgĭto</span></b> ,
			āre, v. freq. a.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to find out by asking</i>, <i>to inquire</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex aliquo, quid, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Capt. 5, 1, 32</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sil. 10, 476</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">qui neque cujatis esset, unquam potuimus multa
					erogitantes sciscere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Att.
					Tr. 625</span></i>
			 (R<i><span class="en">ib. Fragm. Trag. p. 217</span></i>).</div>
